        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-swlist" data-main="software" data-sub="softwarelist">
            <div class="info">
                Every distinct installed program across all devices, with how many devices carry it, which
                findings matched it, whether a license was collected and what the last winget run reported for
                it. The list is built from the inventory already stored on this server - opening it contacts no
                device.
                <br><br>
                The three package actions need a <strong>winget package id</strong>, because winget works by id and
                not by display name. Rows without one show the buttons disabled: the program is installed (the
                inventory proves it) but winget does not manage it, so it can neither be updated nor uninstalled
                this way. <em>Ignore</em> puts the id on the ignore list, so no automatic or batch run upgrades it
                any more. <em>Update everywhere</em> queues exactly this one package on every non-excluded Windows
                device. <em>Uninstall everywhere</em> REMOVES it from every device that has it - devices without it
                report "not installed" rather than a failure - and asks for confirmation; it never runs as a dry run.
                In the "Last winget run" column, <em>ready</em> counts the devices where an update was available,
                <em>ok</em> where it was installed, <em>failed</em> where the install failed (the Details view shows
                the exit code in decimal and hex plus winget's own message) and <em>skipped</em> counts ignored,
                version-less and not-installed entries. Those numbers come from the stored last runs, so start a
                <em>Dry run all devices</em> under Software &gt; Software updates to populate them.
            </div>
            <div class="controls">
                <input type="text" id="swfFilter" class="filter-input" placeholder="Filter by software or publisher..." style="min-width:260px;">
                <button id="swfRefreshBtn" class="small" data-help="swf.refresh">Refresh</button>
                <label class="dlselall" data-help="swf.selectupdatable"><input type="checkbox" id="swfSelectUpdatable"> select updatable</label>
                <span id="swfRunInfo" class="hint"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="table-container">
                <table>
                    <thead><tr>
                        <th style="width:26px;" class="nosort"></th>
                        <th style="cursor:default">Software</th>
                        <th style="cursor:default;width:130px;">Version</th>
                        <th style="cursor:default;width:150px;">Publisher</th>
                        <th style="width:58px;cursor:default">Devices</th>
                        <th style="width:110px;cursor:default">Findings</th>
                        <th style="width:170px;cursor:default">Last winget run</th>
                        <th style="width:60px;cursor:default">License</th>
                        <th style="width:290px;" class="nosort">Actions</th>
                    </tr></thead>
                    <tbody id="swfBody"><tr><td colspan="9" style="color:#888">Loading...</td></tr></tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="controls">
                <button class="green" id="swfUpdateAllBtn" data-help="swf.updateall">Update the selected packages everywhere</button>
            </div>
            <div id="swfMsg"></div>
        </div>
